course: dictionary
lesson: 9629
title: Studbook: a family tree for animals
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A studbook is a record book that lists an animal's parents, grandparents and births. The context tells you what it is for. «Good zoos keep family records called studbooks» means a studbook is a family record.
explain: «Every snow leopard in zoos is written into one giant family tree called a studbook.» The words «called a studbook» name the family tree. So a studbook is a book that shows which animals are related, like a family tree for animals.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «Zoos keep a family tree for rare animals so that they are not too closely related» still makes sense, so you have the right idea. You do not need to know every word; read the words around it.
fact: A studbook is a noun: one studbook, two or more studbooks.
fact: A studbook is an official record book that lists the parents, grandparents and births of animals of one breed.
fact: Horses are the best-known animals with studbooks, but dogs and cattle have them too.
fact: Zoos keep studbooks for rare animals so they can choose mates and keep the animals healthy and varied.
fact: «A studbook records every animal of one kind in zoos: its parents, birth, moves and offspring.» Some go back over a hundred years.
exercise: «A studbook records every animal of one kind in zoos: its parents, birth, moves and offspring.» What does a studbook record? | *An animal's parents, birth, moves and offspring | Only the animal's favourite food | The weather on the day of birth | The price of a ticket to the zoo
exercise: Why do zoos keep studbooks? | *To stop rare animals being too closely related and keep them healthy | To sell tickets | To count how many visitors come | To make the animals run faster
exercise: «A studbook records every animal of one kind in zoos: its parents, birth, moves and offspring.» Find and copy one word that means young animals born to a parent. | parents | *offspring | zoos | records
test: «Some studbooks go back over a hundred years.» How far back can the records go? | A week | *Over a hundred years | Only as far as last year | A month
test: Which animal is a studbook best known for? | Lions only | *Horses | Dogs only | Cattle only
exam: What is a studbook most like? | A menu for lions | A shopping list | *A family tree for animals | A map of a zoo
